## C. AI CHECK — TITLE AND CAPTION ANALYSIS

Use my existing FreeLLM-compatible API for actual analysis.

API endpoint:

https://invalid-ayush-llm.onrender.com/v1/chat/completions

HTTP method: POST

Headers:
- Authorization: Bearer ${FREELLM_API_KEY}
- Content-Type: application/json

Request model:
- model: "auto"

The API uses an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions request format.

A text request can use the following general structure:

{
  "model": "auto",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The concise BrandLens review prompt and the post information"
    }
  ]
}

Read the response from:

choices[0].message.content

Do not call Gemini, Google AI, OpenAI, or an unrelated AI provider as a substitute for my API.

Do not create a fake AI review result and present it as a live API result.

### Text-review prompt

Prepare a concise prompt for the AI containing:
- The post title.
- The caption/details.
- Selected social platform.
- Current user's role.
- Relevant starter guidelines for that role.

Use this instruction:

"You are BrandLens, a concise brand-content assistant. Review the supplied social media post title and caption/details for suitability for the selected platform and role-specific brand guidelines.

Determine whether the content looks suitable, needs small corrections, or needs attention.

Identify only meaningful problems, such as inconsistent terminology, potentially inaccurate details, unsupported claims, misleading promises, unclear messaging, or a mismatch with the supplied guidelines.

Be concise, natural, and practical. Do not produce lengthy explanations, scores, hashtags, marketing essays, or irrelevant advice. Do not invent facts, approvals, sources, or citations. If a factual claim cannot be verified from the supplied information, clearly express uncertainty rather than asserting that it is true or false. Preserve the user's original intent when suggesting corrections."

Request a short structured response with these fields:

{
  "verdict": "looks_good | changes_suggested | needs_attention",
  "briefAnalysis": "One or two concise sentences",
  "suggestion": "One short practical improvement",
  "suggestedTitle": null,
  "suggestedCaption": null,
  "issues": []
}

If correction is unnecessary, suggestedTitle and suggestedCaption should be null where possible.

If correction is needed, return the suggested corrected title and/or caption. Do not rewrite unaffected fields unnecessarily.

The user interface should display:
- Brief Analysis
- Suggestion
- Issues, when applicable
- Suggested title/caption, when applicable
- Apply Suggestion button, when a correction is available
- Recheck button

The user must review and accept suggested changes manually. Never overwrite the title or caption silently.

If the provider returns plain text instead of valid JSON, handle that gracefully. Show the concise response without crashing. Never assume the response is valid JSON.

Keep the AI output concise so that requests remain lightweight.

